    "body": "## Summary\n- `_get_reasoning_from_request` now treats a missing `thinking` kwarg the same way the dsv4/dsv41 encoder does: `SGLANG_DEFAULT_THINKING`.\n- With the cookbook env set, a `/v1/chat/completions` request that omits `reasoning_effort` and `chat_template_kwargs.thinking` is parsed with `force_reasoning`, so the thinking block goes to `reasoning_content` instead of `content`.\n- An explicit `thinking: false` still disables the split. `enable_thinking` parsers are unchanged, because those templates do not read this env.\n\nFixes #45614\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Unit test `test_fallback_explicit_thinking_follows_default_thinking_env` covers env on, env off, explicit true/false, empty kwargs, and that a mimo `enable_thinking` parser ignores the env.\n- [ ] I could not run the SGLang unit suite on this machine (no local checkout of the dependency tree).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39736883311](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39736883311)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39736883146](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39736883146)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39736883374](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39736883374)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
